    "scr_dup": "001",
    "tpa_score_new": "<ul>\n\t<li>Absences and skipping classes deducted Regular Points</li>\n\t<li>Active participation gains extra points scores.</li>\n\t<li>Make-up exams capped at 60 points.</li>\n\t<li>Cheating results in a score of 0.</li>\n</ul>\n",
    "tpa_score_new_en": null,
    "course_pol": "課堂規則\n•Take all examinations (Mid-term exam and final exam).\n•Participate in the weekly discussions.\n•Turn in all work on time.\n•Read the textbook pages listed in the syllabus and found on the weekly assignment pages.\n•Read the weekly lecture and any other supporting document provided by the course instructor.\n•Work the weekly homework problems, and submit them as required by the instructor.",
    "course_pol_en": "•Turn in all work on time.\n•Read the textbook pages listed in the syllabus and found on the weekly assignment pages.\n\nBe sure to carefully read through your student guide to familiarize yourself with the policies, procedures, and resources available to you as a student. If you have any questions or need further clarification, don't hesitate to reach out to your school's administration or academic advisors for assistance.",
    "course_rem": null,
    "course_rem_en": "Honesty: You are expected to submit work that is your own and to properly cite and acknowledge the ideas, words, and contributions of others. Cheating, plagiarism, and fabrication of information are violations of academic integrity and will not be tolerated.\n\nFairness: You are expected to treat your peers, instructors, and members of the academic community with respect and fairness. Collaboration and teamwork are encouraged, but all collaborative work must be conducted in accordance with the guidelines provided by instructors.\n\nResponsibility: You are responsible for familiarizing yourself with and adhering to the academic policies and standards set forth by [Institution Name]. Ignorance of academic integrity principles is not an excuse for unethical behavior.",
